---
description: Imager project coding standards
alwaysApply: true
---

# Code Structure

- One file per concern: transcription, scene_extraction, video_matching, video_composition, config
- Functions under 20 lines, max 2 nesting levels
- No comments, no docstrings - names must be self-explanatory
- Type hints on all functions
- No classes until you need state
- Early returns over nested conditionals

# Configuration

- All constants in config.py
- Zero magic strings or hardcoded values in functions
- Environment variables for secrets via .env file

# Error Handling

- Fail immediately with context: include relevant values in error messages
- No bare except clauses
- Validate inputs at function entry

# Dependencies

- Only add libraries you can explain in one sentence
- Prefer standard library when possible
- Use proven tools: Whisper, MoviePy, FastAPI, sentence-transformers

# Module Independence

- Each module runnable standalone
- Pure functions over stateful classes
- No abstraction until duplication exists
